title: "schema_initialization (0000_create_member_schema)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_drop_tables: DROP TABLE IF EXISTS member.generation_roles CASCADE
    q_drop_tables --> q_drop_team_leaders: DROP TABLE IF EXISTS member.team_leaders CASCADE
    q_drop_team_leaders --> q_drop_relations: DROP TABLE IF EXISTS member.member_team_relations CASCADE
    q_drop_relations --> q_drop_teams: DROP TABLE IF EXISTS member.teams CASCADE
    q_drop_teams --> q_drop_members: DROP TABLE IF EXISTS member.members CASCADE
    q_drop_members --> q_drop_schema: DROP SCHEMA IF EXISTS member CASCADE
    q_drop_schema --> q_create_schema: CREATE SCHEMA IF NOT EXISTS member
    q_create_schema --> q_grant_usage: GRANT USAGE ON SCHEMA member TO postgres, anon, authenticated, service_role
    q_grant_usage --> q_default_tables: ALTER DEFAULT PRIVILEGES GRANT ALL ON TABLES
    q_default_tables --> q_default_functions: ALTER DEFAULT PRIVILEGES GRANT ALL ON FUNCTIONS
    q_default_functions --> q_default_sequences: ALTER DEFAULT PRIVILEGES GRANT ALL ON SEQUENCES
    q_default_sequences --> [*]: schema ready

    note right of q_drop_tables
        INV-001: Tables must be dropped in reverse dependency order to avoid FK violations
        INV-002: CASCADE ensures dependent objects are also dropped
    end note

    note right of q_grant_usage
        INV-003: All four roles (postgres, anon, authenticated, service_role) receive schema usage
        INV-004: Default privileges ensure future objects inherit grants automatically
    end note
